# Base apt packages — every machine (desktop, server, wsl, wsl-work).
# Everything here must be acceptable on a company machine: no personal-use
# tooling. Entries with a licence or policy caveat carry it as a comment so the
# decision stays traceable (docs/setup/wsl-work.md). Anything that is not
# acceptable goes in personal.list.
# One package per line. Blank lines and # comments ignored.
# Installed by: setup/modules/00-apt-base.sh
# Docs:         docs/setup/ubuntu-base.md

# Shell & editors
zsh
vim
neovim
# emacs: not here. Its builds conflict with each other, so the right one is
# picked per profile: emacs-nox (server.list, wsl.list), emacs-pgtk
# (desktop.list). See docs/setup/emacs.md.

# Terminal multiplexing & monitoring
tmux
htop
btop
# smartmontools: smartctl for disk health. Little use inside WSL2 or a VM
# (virtual disks), harmless there.
smartmontools

# Network
# iftop, ngrep: packet capture. Kept on wsl-work on purpose (pen testing /
# debugging, no endpoint-protection agent on WSL as of 2026-10). Use only on
# traffic and targets you are authorised for. Both free licences (GPL / BSD-style).
# In WSL2 they only see the virtual NIC, not the Windows host's traffic.
iftop
ngrep
lsof

# Version control
git
git-lfs
gh

# Transfer & backup
wget
curl
# aria2: chunked/concurrent downloads of large files (e.g. ISOs). GPL-2.0, free
# for business use. It can also speak BitTorrent: never use that for anything
# but legitimate distribution (e.g. an official ISO torrent). bin/aria2c-d wraps it.
aria2
rsync
# restic: BSD-2, free for business use. At work it must only ever talk to
# work-owned repositories and credentials; no personal backup targets, no
# personal repo passwords, nothing from this repo's personal backup setup.
restic
# Previously only a gnome-shell dependency (auto); see desktop.list.
sshfs
gnupg
ca-certificates

# Pagers & syntax highlighting
less
bat
multitail
python3-pygments

# Search & find
fd-find
fzf
ripgrep
# TODO look into ripgrep-all

# Data wrangling
jq
gawk
parallel

# Key & certificate management
sqv

# Archives
unzip
zip
# 7zip, not p7zip-full: the latter is now only a virtual name provided by 7zip.
# dpkg-query never reports a virtual package as installed, so using it here
# would make every run reinstall it and report a change forever. It happens to
# work on machines that upgraded through the transitional package — i.e. it
# would only break on a fresh box.
7zip

# Python
python3-pip
python3-venv
python-is-python3

# Development tools
shellcheck

# Cron & scheduling
# cronic wraps a cron job so output is mailed only on failure. Crontabs
# reference it directly, so its absence breaks them *silently* — a desktop
# purge removed it from saito on 2026-09-26 and took the backups down for two
# weeks unnoticed. Tiny (21 kB installed, no deps beyond a shell).
# NOTE: it reports by mailing root, which nobody reads. It is not alerting;
# that is the ntfy heartbeat in the backup jobs.
cronic

# File maintenance
jdupes
rmlint
# https://github.com/dundee/gdu/tree/master - A fast disk usage analyzer written in Go
gdu

# Other
rename
# ghostscript: PDF processing (hard on Windows without proprietary tools).
# AGPL-3.0 (Artifex). Running it as a local CLI tool imposes no obligations;
# do NOT embed it in a product or expose it as a network service without
# checking the AGPL / Artifex commercial licence. Some company licence policies
# blocklist AGPL — confirm once with legal/IT if in doubt.
ghostscript
